-- Update skill-management system skill to include all 6 skill tools
-- Adds: grepSkills, readSkillFile, executeSkill to the documentation

UPDATE "skills"
SET "files" = '[{"path":"SKILL.md","content":"# Skill Management\n\nManage skills - discover, read, execute, and create custom skills.\n\n## Available Tools\n\n### Discovery Tools\n- **grepSkills**: Search across all skill files for content matching a pattern\n- **readSkillFile**: Read a specific skill file (supports partial reading with offset/limit)\n\n### Execution Tool\n- **executeSkill**: Execute any tool using CLI-style syntax (the primary way to invoke tools)\n\n### CRUD Tools (User Skills Only)\n- **createSkill**: Create a new user skill with documentation files\n- **updateSkill**: Update an existing user skill\n- **deleteSkill**: Delete a user skill permanently\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **System skills** (like web-research, project-management) are read-only\n- Only **user skills** can be created/updated/deleted\n- Each skill requires at least one file (typically SKILL.md)\n\n## Using executeSkill\n\nThe executeSkill tool lets you run any available tool using CLI-style commands:\n\n### Syntax\n```\nexecuteSkill --command \"toolName --arg1 value1 --arg2 \\\"value with spaces\\\"\"\n```\n\n### Examples\n```\nexecuteSkill --command \"webSearch --query \\\"React 19 features\\\"\"\nexecuteSkill --command \"createTask --projectId abc123 --title \\\"New task\\\" --priority high\"\nexecuteSkill --command \"getTime --timezone \\\"America/New_York\\\"\"\nexecuteSkill --command \"listProjects\"\n```\n\n### Supported Value Types\n- Strings: `--arg \"value\"` or `--arg value`\n- Numbers: `--count 10`\n- Booleans: `--verbose true` or `--verbose false`\n- JSON: `--data ''[{\"key\": \"value\"}]''`\n\n## Discovering Skills\n\n### Search skill content\n```\ngrepSkills --pattern \"API\"\ngrepSkills --pattern \"authentication\" --skillKey \"my-skill\"\n```\n\n### Read a skill file\n```\nreadSkillFile --skillKey \"web-research\" --filePath \"SKILL.md\"\nreadSkillFile --skillKey \"project-management\" --filePath \"references/task-states.md\"\nreadSkillFile --skillKey \"my-skill\" --filePath \"SKILL.md\" --offset 0 --limit 50\n```\n\n## Creating a Skill\n\n```\ncreateSkill --key \"my-skill\" --name \"My Custom Skill\" --description \"A helpful skill\" --files ''[{\"path\":\"SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"# My Skill\\n\\nDocumentation here...\"}]''\n```\n\n### Key Requirements\n\n- Must be unique across your skills\n- Lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens only\n- Maximum 64 characters\n\n### Files Array\n\n- At least 1 file, maximum 20 files\n- Each file needs `path` and `content` properties\n- Path max 255 characters\n- Content max 500KB per file\n\n## Updating a Skill\n\n```\nupdateSkill --id \"uuid-here\" --name \"Updated Name\"\nupdateSkill --id \"uuid-here\" --files ''[{\"path\":\"SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"New content...\"}]''\n```\n\nYou can update:\n- `key` - Change the skill identifier\n- `name` - Change display name\n- `description` - Change description\n- `files` - Replace all files (full replacement, not merge)\n\n## Deleting a Skill\n\n```\ndeleteSkill --id \"uuid-here\"\n```\n\n**Warning**: Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.\n"},{"path":"references/skill-structure.md","content":"# Skill File Structure\n\n## Recommended Structure\n\n```\nmy-skill/\n├── SKILL.md              # Main documentation (required)\n└── references/           # Optional additional docs\n    ├── examples.md\n    └── troubleshooting.md\n```\n\n## SKILL.md Template\n\n```markdown\n# Skill Name\n\nBrief description of what this skill helps with.\n\n## Available Tools\n\n- **toolName**: What it does\n- **anotherTool**: What it does\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### Workflow 1\n1. Step one\n2. Step two\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- Tip 1\n- Tip 2\n```\n\n## Validation Limits\n\n| Field | Limit |\n|-------|-------|\n| Max files per skill | 20 |\n| Max path length | 255 characters |\n| Max content per file | 500KB |\n| Key length | 1-64 characters |\n| Name length | 1-255 characters |\n| Description length | 1-1000 characters |\n\n## Key Naming Convention\n\n- Use lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens only\n- Be descriptive but concise\n- Examples: `my-api`, `team-workflow`, `data-processing`\n"}]'::jsonb,
    "updated_at" = NOW()
WHERE "key" = 'skill-management' AND "is_system" = true;
